{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc, beating RNA-only (0.485) and image-only (0.208), confirming RNA is the dominant signal and that adding image via concat provides a modest but real boost. However, we have only tested one fusion method (concat) in the multimodal setting. Question: config_006 is identical to config_002 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, making this a clean single-variable A/B comparison that isolates the effect of the fusion mechanism. Why best next: Under a limited budget, the most informative experiment is one that changes exactly one design axis from the current best result. The fusion method is a fundamental architectural choice that will determine how we combine the (dominant) RNA and (weak) image streams; knowing whether weighted fusion helps or hurts relative to concat directly guides all subsequent multimodal experiments and prevents us from carrying a suboptimal fusion forward into more complex multiprofile/aggregation settings."
}

